course: dictionary
lesson: 10890
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer wants. «She plays first violin» is about a person playing in a band, not about an object.
explain: A violin is a musical instrument with four strings. You hold it under your chin and play it with a bow, or pluck the strings with your fingers. To check, swap in the meaning: «She plays first violin» still makes sense if you think "she plays the first violin part in the band".
explain: Words in a group can give you clues too. The violin, viola, cello and double bass are all string instruments. The violin is the smallest and highest-sounding, so the other words in the group help you picture size and sound.
fact: A violin is a musical instrument with four strings.
fact: You play a violin with a bow or by plucking the strings.
fact: «Violin» can also mean the part a violinist plays in a band or orchestra, as in «She plays first violin».
fact: The violin is the smallest and highest-sounding of the string family: violin, viola, cello and double bass.
fact: Shorter or tighter strings give a higher note.
exercise: «She plays first violin in the school band.» What does violin mean here? | A loud drum | A song sung by the whole class | A wooden box for carrying instruments | *The part a violinist plays in a band
exercise: Which instrument is the smallest and highest-sounding of the string family? | Viola | Double bass | *Violin | Cello
exercise: «Shorter or tighter strings give a higher note.» What makes a note higher? | Playing it more quietly | *Shorter or tighter strings | Longer, looser strings | Holding the instrument upside down
test: How do you play a violin? | Stand it on the floor | *With a bow, or by plucking the strings | Hit it with sticks | Blow into it
test: «She has violin lessons after school.» What does violin mean here? | A small wooden box | A type of drum | *A musical instrument with four strings | A kind of pen
exam: In the string family, which order goes from highest to lowest? | *Violin, viola, cello, double bass | Cello, violin, double bass, viola | Viola, violin, cello, double bass | Double bass, cello, viola, violin
